@JamesNK built from the current main: [System.Net.Http-SwappedTelemetry.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16092411/System.Net.Http-SwappedTelemetry.zip), PTAL if it does the job!

Note that the [naive change](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/compare/main...antonfirsov:enable-exemplars-01) breaks the ability of registering metrics enrichment callbacks on `System.Net.Http.HttpRequestOut.Stop` DaignosticSource events, unless we are willing to commit to a refactor that merges the two handlers so we can reorder things in complicated ways. I would prefer taking the breaking change instead, since I doubt there are many users doing enrichment together with DiagnosticListener. In fact, metrics enrichment seems to be a vastly unused feature. Thoughts?

It may also break other stuff, didn't have a chance yet to investigate the impact fully.
